window.docContents[219].resolve({"/Some-examples/#Formalization-of-stochastic-iterative-optimization-algorithm--Some-examples--CMA-ES--The-original-CMA-ES--Ranking-a-generation":{"contents":"As LeanGO maximizes objective functions, a point of a generation is better than another one if its evaluation is greater, ties being broken by index:\n\n\n\nRather than sorting the generation, which would require to manipulate a permutation of \\{1, \\dots, \\lambda\\}, we count, for each point, the number of points that are better than it:\n\n\n\nThe rank of the k-th point of a generation, i.e. the number of points of that generation\nthat are CMAES.better than it.\n\nAs better is a strict total order, this is a bijection between the points of the generation and \\{0, \\dots, \\lambda - 1\\}: the rank of a point is its index in the sorted generation, the best point having rank 0.\n\n","context":"Formalization of stochastic iterative optimization algorithm\u0009Some examples\u0009CMA-ES\u0009The original CMA-ES","header":"2.5.1.1. Ranking a generation","id":"/Some-examples/#Formalization-of-stochastic-iterative-optimization-algorithm--Some-examples--CMA-ES--The-original-CMA-ES--Ranking-a-generation"}});